d equal to page id. We must avoid inventing product names; centralize.\n\nBetter design: constants:\n- $ExePath = env OSAKA_WIN_EXE or \"windows/bin/.../OsakaConnect.exe\"\n- $WindowTitle = env OSAKA_WIN_WINDOW_TITLE or \"Osaka...\" \n- nav items as ordered pairs: @{Name=\"连接\"; PageId=\"W1\"}, @{Name=\"设置\"; PageId=\"W4\"}\n- page id element: AutomationId == PageId (documented assumption). Alternative fallback check any element Name/AutomationId containing page id, visible.\n\nThe assertion \"页面标识与设计稿编号一致\" maybe page has text \"W1\"/\"W4\"? Hmm. The acceptance says \"UI 测试断言页面标识与设计稿编号一致\". Page identifier likely an AutomationId. Use UIA to find element with AutomationId or Name equal to W1. This is reasonable and centralized.\n\nA14: windows/ under only *.csproj/*.cs/*.xaml. Scan files recursively, excluding bin/obj? Acceptance says \"windows/ 下只允许 *.csproj/*.cs/*.xaml\". Strictly bin/obj would contain dlls, so must exclude build outputs bin/obj or run in clean checkout before build. For CI, scan source tree excluding bin/obj (and maybe .git). Comment shortcut. Also check docs/architecture.md stack section? A14 also says another check docs arch, but task scope specifically \"A14（windows/ 下只允许 *.csproj/*.cs/*.xaml）\". Only that.\n\nA17: windows source (cs/xaml/csproj? \"客户端源码\") must not contain literal \"Line 01\" or \"OSA · 01\". Grep .cs/.xaml/.csproj files. Resource files allowed per acceptance, but task says \"windows/ 源码不含线路字面量 Line 01 / OSA · 01\". Scan .cs/.xaml (source). Could include .csproj? no. Use Select-String -SimpleMatch.\n\nA1: run exe --self-test; exit code 0 within timeout. Start-Process -Wait -PassThru. WPF app self-test should exit on its own. Timeout handling in PowerShell is awkward. Could use Start-Process then WaitForExit(timeout ms); if not exit, kill and fail. Good.\n\nAlso output \"待测：模块未交付\" when windows/ absent (or exe not found? If source exists but exe not built — that's a test environment failure, not \"not delivered\"). The instruction: product code not delivered → output skip. windows/ absent in our worktree. If windows/ exists but exe missing, likely CI build issue → fail with clear message. Perhaps script has optional -SkipIfNotBuilt? Keep simple: absent windows/ → skip; exe missing → fail (CI should build). But if writers deliver source but CI hasn't built and user runs script manually, fail with clear message \"exe 不存在：先构建\". That's a genuine failure at CI. Fine.\n\nStructure: functions + tests, exit 1 on any failure. Use exit 0 and clear messages.\n\nAlso \"一个 xUnit 测试项目草稿或说明\" — choose 说明 (explanation) to avoid extra code? The task says \"可用 pwsh 脚本（smoke.ps1）+ 一个 xUnit 测试项目草稿或说明\". A short README.md explaining decisions, constants to align, CI command. Probably good and minimal: smoke.ps1 + README.md. But maybe a xUnit draft is expected for A2/A16 UI test? Powershell UIA covers it. An explanation is permitted. I'll do README.md with alignment notes.\n\nNeed pytest? No, Windows .NET, use pwsh. We cannot run pwsh locally maybe? Check pwsh available. On Linux maybe not. The script targets windows-latest and \"脚本顶部标注待 CI\". We should syntax-check if pwsh installed. Let's check.\n\nAlso need tests/INDEX.md? Only allowed tests/windows/win-shell/. So no.\n\nLet me verify shared files for line literals? Not needed.\n\nCheck whether pwsh exists.","signature":"3b72f9ff-0db5-4240-ad43-9c64c80c5553"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1018,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":16256,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"befe153c-b82d-4792-9ae9-6d63c8cbba56","uuid":"99b1c0e7-2b47-406d-99be-2fad53c3a32d","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:02:26.329Z","thinking_duration_ms":9014,"thinking_display":"updates"}
