{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"c8e06f93-ff4c-4351-9f74-04d0509e8a72","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Need check pwsh separately; tool rejected compound. Not critical. Let's design script carefully.\n\nPotential concern: UI Automation in CI on windows-latest — WPF app can be queried via UIAutomation even in non-interactive session? GitHub Actions windows-latest runs in an interactive-ish session (RDP disabled but desktop exists). UIA usually works for WPF. Use System.Windows.Automation.\n\nSelecting nav element: nav items likely buttons with Content \"连接\"/\"设置\". Find by Name. For page id, assume element AutomationId == \"W1\"/\"W4\". But better to check any element AutomationId or Name exactly page id. Need find visible element. Implement helper Find-Element($root, $pageId) using property condition on AutomationId OR (ORCondition for AutomationId/Name). Then filter Current.IsOffscreen -eq false. Wait up to N seconds.\n\nClick nav: find button by Name exactly nav label, invoke pattern (InvokePattern) else select? WPF Button supports InvokePattern. Sidebar nav might be ListBoxItem/RadioButton. Use InvokePattern if available, else SelectionItemPattern.Select, else click via mouse coordinates? Mouse click via UIA won't work in session maybe but SendInput works. Keep fallback: use InvokePattern, then SelectionItemPattern, then SetFocus + send Enter? Simplicity: Invoke then Select. Comment pending alignment.\n\nPage identifier maybe text in header: e.g., TextBlock with Name \"W1\"? Name of TextBlock is its text. If the UI displays \"连接\" title, identifier W1 might be AutomationId assigned by writer. The brief says \"页标识与设计稿编号一致\" — so writer should expose W1/W4 as identifier. We can search AutomationId/Name exactly. Good.\n\nA17 grep: use Get-ChildItem -Recurse -File -Include *.cs,*.xaml under windows (exclude bin/obj). Select-String -SimpleMatch -Pattern 'Line 01','OSA · 01'. Note OSA · 01 has middle dot U+00B7 and spaces. In PowerShell pattern strings fine; file encoding? Select-String handles UTF-8 default? Windows PowerShell 5.1 Select-String default encoding detection with BOM issues; pwsh 7 defaults UTF-8. CI uses pwsh. Good.\n\nA14 allow list: Only *.csproj/*.cs/*.xaml. What about .sln? A14 strict says only those, so solution file would be violation, and Windows client typically needs .sln. But acceptance says \"windows/、admin/ 下只允许 *.csproj/*.cs/*.xaml\". So writer should avoid .sln (or CI workflow builds csproj). Follow acceptance strictly. Exclusions: bin/obj (build outputs), maybe nested .git none. Also exclude hidden? Keep bin/obj exclusion with comment. Test also should catch stray files at root. Good.\n\nWhat about `windows/` source absent but branch not delivered? skip.\n\nSmoke A1: Need exe path. Candidate: env OSAKA_WIN_EXE, else search windows/**/bin/**/*.exe? Better: writer should specify. Define $ExePath default \"\" and if empty, auto-discover under windows/ for *.exe excluding obj; but ambiguity with multiple exes. Task says \"入口 exe 路径...放顶部变量，待写手交付后对齐\". So constant with placeholder path and env override. If not found → fail with message \"待写手交付后对齐\". But CI cannot align until writer edits? The writer is told not to touch tests. Hmm. Actually test writer delivers script; path must work once product delivered. Auto-discovery is more robust: look for windows/**/*.csproj, derive assembly name, expected exe at bin/Release/net8.0-windows/<assembly>.exe or Debug. Or simply search windows/**/bin/**/<name>.exe. But \"入口 exe 路径...放顶部变量\". Provide $ExePath override + fallback discovery. Reasonable small.\n\nYet product not delivered now, so script exits skip before any. Once delivered, CI builds; smoke must find exe. Auto-discovery:\n- If OSAKA_WIN_EXE set, use it.\n- Else get *.csproj; for each, parse <AssemblyName> or filename; search windows/**/bin/**/$name.exe, sort by LastWriteTime desc, pick first. Simpler: Get-ChildItem windows -Recurse -Filter *.exe | where full path matches bin and not obj, exclude testhost? but could pick tests exe. Prefer csproj assembly name.\n\nUI automation also needs window process. We launch app normally without --self-test (which exits immediately). Start-Process, wait for MainWindowHandle, then UIA root from handle. In CI no visible desktop? windows-latest runners do have a desktop session in GitHub-hosted runners. WPF apps can start. UIA can attach. This is standard.\n\nBut wait: A1 smoke uses --self-test; A2/A16 UI test launches normally, navigates, then closes app. Need kill process finally.\n\nTimeout logic: Wait for MainWindowHandle up to 20s.\n\nAlso \"页面标识\" assertion possibly reading an accessible name. Implement Find-PageMarker scanning all descendants where AutomationId or Name equals id AND not offscreen. Might match nav button if nav button contains \"W1\"? Name likely \"连接\". Fine.\n\nWrite functions:\n- Skip-Module($why): Write-Host \"待测：模块未交付（$why）\"; exit 0\n- Assert helper: $script:Failures list; Check($cond,$msg).\n\nSince PowerShell `exit` at top-level.\n\nScript param: maybe -WindowsRoot default repo-relative. Use $PSScriptRoot/../../../windows. Compute repo root = Resolve-Path (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot \"../../..\"). tests/windows/win-shell → ../../.. = repo root. Good.\n\nSource scan functions.\n\nIf windows dir exists:\nA14 scan.\nA17 scan.\nA1 smoke: require exe; if no exe → fail? Maybe skip with \"待测：构建产物未就绪\"? CI expects build before. Fail is correct because A1 needs build. But script itself maybe runs build? Task says \"本机不装 JDK/SDK/.NET、不跑构建；脚本顶部标注'待 CI'\". So script runs in CI after build. Exe missing → failure with instruction. Fine.\n\nA2/A16 UI: launch exe, UIA. If UIA fails due to environment maybe failure. Fine.\n\nSummarize and exit 1 if failures.\n\nxUnit \"说明\": README.md in tests/windows/win-shell/. Include why no xUnit project (would need dependency/CI setup; UIA from pwsh), how to align constants, run command, pending items.\n\nWait, \"一个 xUnit 测试项目草稿或说明\" — README satisfies \"说明\".\n\nShould we add a test for the smoke script itself? Ponytail says new non-trivial script needs a small test or assert-based self-check. The script itself is the test; no need.\n\nLocal verification: can't run pwsh? Let's check separately.","signature":"c8e06f93-ff4c-4351-9f74-04d0509e8a72"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1433,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":18688,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"befe153c-b82d-4792-9ae9-6d63c8cbba56","uuid":"08fb1b44-9525-4359-9b66-561d6c3e6237","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:02:38.664Z","thinking_duration_ms":10901,"thinking_display":"updates"}
